<%# locals: (budget:) %>
<%# The month view's Available bar and pill at each level, drawn from sample figures, and the Show details toggle. %>
<% levels = [
     { name: "Plenty", note: "$400.00 of $500.00 left", line: { assigned: 500, spent: 100 } },
     { name: "A little", note: "$20.00 of $500.00 left", line: { assigned: 500, spent: 480 } },
     { name: "Overspent", note: "$30.00 over", line: { assigned: 100, spent: 130 } },
     { name: "None", note: "Nothing to spend and no Spends", line: {} }
   ].map do |level|
     figures = { carried_over: 0, assigned: 0, spent: 0, refunded: 0, reallocated: 0 }.merge(level[:line]).transform_values { |amount| BigDecimal(amount) }
     level.merge(line: Budget::Month::EnvelopeLine.new(envelope: nil, **figures, available: figures[:assigned] - figures[:spent]))
   end %>
<section id="available-bars" aria-labelledby="available-bars-heading" class="space-y-4 border-t border-base-300 pt-6">
  <h2 id="available-bars-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold">Available bar, Available pill and Show details</h2>
  <p class="text-base-content/70">The bar sits under the envelope's name, as wide as its column, with no word: its colour and length say plenty from a little, and Overspent is a dashed line. The Available figure is in a pill tinted for the level, with an icon for each, and Overspent says so in a word under it, on the bar's line, so every row is the same height. An envelope with nothing to spend has no bar and a plain pill.</p>

  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Level</th>
          <th scope="col" class="text-right">Available</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <% levels.each do |level| %>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="align-top leading-8">
              <span class="text-base font-medium"><%= level[:name] %></span> <span class="text-sm text-base-content/70">(<%= level[:note] %>)</span>
              <%= render "components/available_bar", line: level[:line] %>
            </td>
            <td class="text-right align-top leading-8 tabular-nums"><%= render "components/available_pill", line: level[:line], budget: budget %></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      <% end %>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="text-base-content/70">The toggle shows or hides the table's Carried over, Refunded and Reallocated, and says what hiding them means. Both of its hints and both of its labels are always there, so nothing moves when it changes.</p>
  <div data-controller="month-details" data-action="turbo:morph@document->month-details#sync">
    <%= render "months/details_toggle" %>
  </div>
</section>
